## 1. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY

An exhaustive technical, architectural, product, security, and deployment audit was conducted across the entire **Telangana Jyothi** codebase.

The repository consists of a multi-project structure:
1. **`telangana-jyothi-spot-news`**: Next.js 16 (React 19) App Router web application serving as the central Admin Control Panel Single-Page Application (SPA), dynamic article preview renderer (`/p/[id]`), REST API server (`/api/admin/*`, `/api/mobile/*`), and RSS news scraping aggregator.
2. **`telangana_jyothi_shorts`**: Cross-platform Flutter mobile application (Android/iOS/Web) featuring vertical video news reels, localized news feeds, reporter news publishing workflows, and a gamified earnings wallet.
3. **`telangana_jyothi_expo`**: Abandoned/scaffolded empty folder containing only unpopulated `node_modules`.

### Overall System Maturity: **BETA CANDIDATE / PRODUCTION UNSAFE**
While the domain modeling in Prisma and the core Flutter UI features demonstrate high design intent, the codebase suffered from **critical security credential leaks**, **unhandled deployment container crashes**, **missing directory initializations**, and **empty stub API folders**.

